> What does it take to make a low-level wizard survive? It's almost
> impossible to find armor to match the level of monsters I encounter
> without giving up spellcasting (which kinda defeats the purpose of a
> wizard). Are there some tricks that I'm ignorant of?
> 
It sounds like your gaining levels faster than your diving. Even if
not, wizards do have equip problems. The generals tips apply to
keeping low level wizzies alive.

Use your pet. Let him handle more kills and let him get buffed up. 

Collect daggers to throw. This helps conserve spell points for when
you get swarmed. 

When in doubt, run. Fight in choke points.

Use the E word.

If you find some metal body armor, and it turns out to be +5, don't be
afraid to wear it until you can find something to replace it. 
(protection, other non metal gear, a kick ass offensive spell.) This
is another reason to throw daggers.



